From d8fd3856ee7c110fc501a2946e8ad27cabd53769 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:22:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] [jakompiled] web: OpenGOAL's OpenGL renderer on WebGL 2

- WebGL 2 context (GLES 3.0) through SDL3 on an OffscreenCanvas in main()'s pthread
- glad loads every GL 4.3 entry point the browser has; web/gl_web.cpp fills in the 13 the
  renderer uses that WebGL 2 lacks (1D textures as 2D, 8_8_8_8_REV, multi-draw, texture size
  queries and readback, primitive restart...) and filters desktop-only capabilities
- shaders: GLSL ES 3.00 versions generated by web/glsl_es.py (glslang + SPIRV-Cross) in
  shaders_es/<game>, embedded in gk
- no MSAA (no multisample textures in WebGL 2); mip framebuffers use attachment 0
- without extracted data (GAME.fr3) the renderer starts with an empty common level
